BT 1 0 0 1 54 689.8898 Tm (WORKING DRAFT - NOT READY FOR SUBMISSION. Controlled synthetic evidence is included; real TabPFN-3, TabICLv2, and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 54 679.8898 Tm (TabFM experiments remain mandatory.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 15.6 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 654.8898 Tm (Abstract) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 634.8898 Tm (Tabular foundation models \(TFMs\) are usually trained as univariate predictors but are increasingly composed autoregressively for) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 623.6898 Tm (multivariate inference. Recent work shows that contemporary TFMs can violate marginalization and factorization consistency: direct) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 612.4898 Tm (marginals and conditional predictions obtained from the same frozen model need not correspond to one joint distribution. We study) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 601.2898 Tm (post-hoc reconciliation of these incompatible predictions without retraining. CoRe-TFM treats p\(A|X\), p\(B|X\), p\(A|B,X\), and p\(B|A,X\)) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 590.0898 Tm (as four probabilistic views of a categorical target pair. Hard CoRe projects a consensus joint onto the transportation polytope defined) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 578.8898 Tm (by the direct marginals. Soft CoRe relaxes marginal preservation and admits generalized Sinkhorn-style multiplicative updates.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 567.6898 Tm (Selective CoRe uses validation data to decide whether reconciliation should be applied. Controlled experiments with exact) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 556.4898 Tm (ground-truth joints across 10 seeds show that coherence is not equivalent to probabilistic correctness: the preferred method changes) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 545.2898 Tm (with dependence, sample size, feature dimension, class cardinality, and imbalance. A final real-model benchmark on TabPFN-3,) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 534.0898 Tm (TabICLv2, and TabFM remains required before submission.) Tj T* ET
BT /F4 8.8 Tf 10.56 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 517.8898 Tm (Keywords: tabular foundation models; probabilistic consistency; probability reconciliation; calibration; uncertainty quantification;) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 506.6898 Tm (Sinkhorn scaling) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 15.6 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 487.4898 Tm (1 Introduction) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 467.4898 Tm (Tabular foundation models such as TabPFN, TabICL, and TabFM perform in-context prediction from labeled context sets and expose) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 456.2898 Tm (probability predictions without fitting a conventional task-specific model. Their probabilistic outputs make them attractive for) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 445.0898 Tm (uncertainty quantification, conditional density estimation, imputation, sequential sampling, and other multivariate uses.) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 428.8898 Tm (A difficulty appears when a model designed for univariate prediction is used as a multivariate building block. For two categorical) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 417.6898 Tm (targets A and B, the same frozen TFM can provide direct marginals p\(A|X\) and p\(B|X\), plus conditionals p\(A|B,X\) and p\(B|A,X\). If) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 406.4898 Tm (these four views came from one coherent joint distribution, the two chain-rule factorizations would agree and marginalization would) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 395.2898 Tm (recover the direct predictions. Recent work documents systematic violations of these requirements in contemporary TFMs and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 384.0898 Tm (explicitly identifies post-hoc reconciliation as an open direction.) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 367.8898 Tm (Coherence alone is not enough: any single normalized joint distribution is internally coherent by construction. The research problem is) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 356.6898 Tm (therefore to select a coherent joint that does not destroy useful predictive information. We ask whether reconciliation improves proper) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 345.4898 Tm (scoring, calibration, conditional predictions, and distance to known truth, and whether validation data can identify situations in which) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 334.2898 Tm (repair should be skipped.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 315.0898 Tm (1.1 Research questions and contributions) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 50 297.0898 Tm (-) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 297.0898 Tm (RQ1 - Reconciliation: how can four incompatible TFM prediction views be combined into a single joint without retraining the) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 286.2898 Tm (foundation model?) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 50 273.4898 Tm (-) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 273.4898 Tm (RQ2 - Correctness: when the true conditional joint is known, does reconciliation move predictions closer to truth or can it worsen an) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 262.6898 Tm (already good ordering?) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 50 249.8898 Tm (-) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 249.8898 Tm (RQ3 - Selectivity: can validation evidence identify a consistency dividend and avoid regimes that impose a consistency tax?) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 50 237.0898 Tm (-) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 237.0898 Tm (Contribution 1: a TFM-specific four-view convex reconciliation formulation with hard and soft marginal constraints.) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 50 224.2898 Tm (-) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 224.2898 Tm (Contribution 2: generalized Sinkhorn-style updates that make the soft objective fast enough for batched post-processing.) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 50 211.4898 Tm (-) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 211.4898 Tm (Contribution 3: a selective validation protocol plus known-truth synthetic benchmarks measuring coherence, fidelity, calibration, and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 200.6898 Tm (proper scores.) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 50 187.8898 Tm (-) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 187.8898 Tm (Contribution 4: negative evidence showing that a simple label-free directional-defect heuristic is not a reliable universal repair trigger.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 15.6 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 172.0898 Tm (2 Related work and novelty boundary) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 152.0898 Tm (The work sits at the intersection of tabular foundation models, probabilistic reliability, incompatible conditional distributions, and KL) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 140.8898 Tm (projection. Recent TFM studies increasingly evaluate calibration and uncertainty rather than accuracy alone. Compatibility of) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 129.6898 Tm (separately specified conditional distributions is much older than foundation models, and iterative proportional fitting, Bregman) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 118.4898 Tm (projection, and generalized or unbalanced Sinkhorn scaling are established optimization tools. Post-hoc adjustment of TFM) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 107.2898 Tm (probabilities also exists for other failure modes such as label shift.) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 91.08976 Tm (Accordingly, CoRe-TFM does not claim to invent probability compatibility, KL projection, Sinkhorn scaling, or generic post-hoc TFM) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 79.88976 Tm (correction. Its intended contribution is the four-view TFM reconciliation formulation, the selective deployment protocol, and an) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 68.68976 Tm (empirical characterization of the coherence-fidelity-calibration trade-off raised by the newly documented TFM inconsistency problem.) Tj T* ET
