BT 1 0 0 1 48 507.4898 Tm (Hard CoRe trusts the direct marginals and reconciles only the dependence structure by projecting the geometric consensus onto the) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 496.2898 Tm (transportation polytope with row sums p_A and column sums p_B:) Tj T* ET
BT /F5 8.5 Tf 10.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 144.6378 480.0898 Tm (Q_H = argmin_Q KL\(Q || M_w\)  subject to Q_A=p_A and Q_B=p_B.) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 460.0898 Tm (The feasible set is non-empty because the independent joint p_A p_B^T always satisfies the marginal constraints. Under positive) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 448.8898 Tm (support, strict convexity yields a unique optimum. Iterative proportional fitting provides the numerical solution, and direct marginal) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 437.6898 Tm (decisions remain exactly unchanged.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 418.4898 Tm (4.3 Soft four-view CoRe) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 400.4898 Tm (Exact marginal preservation can preserve a marginal error. Soft CoRe therefore optimizes) Tj T* ET
BT /F5 8.5 Tf 10.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 98.7378 384.2898 Tm (min_Q w KL\(Q||J1\)+\(1-w\) KL\(Q||J2\)+lambda_A KL\(Q_A||p_A\)+lambda_B KL\(Q_B||p_B\).) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 9.2 Tf 11.04 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 364.2898 Tm (The KL chain rule decomposes each joint term into a marginal term plus an expected conditional term. Consequently the objective) Tj T* ET
